From 8d9b328b48cf76e693daadefede78afc363ab569 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 12:38:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00825/11171] [outer-loop] #3 in-loop energy feasibility gate:
 NO lift (3 seeds) -- honest negative

Energy as a per-step greedy feasibility gate gave mean_delta +0.0007 over greedy
(seeds 0/1/2: +0.0020/0.0/0.0). Joins descent and rerank as energy-uses that do
NOT add generative value on Sudoku.

TWO CONFOUNDS (stated honestly, this is preliminary):
 1. Underpowered base: this refiner only reached ~3% solve (greedy 0.022-0.039)
    vs v4's ~18% -- n_train=10000/4000-steps undertrained it, so little headroom
    for a gate to help.
 2. Structural: gated grids still average ~7.7 violations -- a GREEDY feasibility
    gate cannot satisfy Sudoku CSP without backtracking, and it only blocks NEW
    conflicts, so it faithfully propagates the refiner's confident-but-wrong early
    cells instead of fixing them.

Mechanism read: the simplest in-loop gate is structurally insufficient (greedy
!= CSP solver) and the test was underpowered. Rather than sink another window into
a backtracking gate (at which point it's a solver using the refiner as a heuristic,
not 'the refiner generating'), this MOTIVATES #4: energy belongs at TRAINING time
(teacher/process-reward, shaping the amortized map) -- where amortized inference
wins -- not at inference time (descent/rerank/gate all fail).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
